>> title: Spinach Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: spinach, bacon, mushrooms, egg, warm dressing
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: spinach salad, wilted spinach salad, warm spinach salad, spinach salad with hot bacon dressing, german spinach salad, bacon dressing salad
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the dressing has about a minute at the right heat, and spinach hit twice goes from wilted to stewed

>> step: render 8 min
Render @thick-cut bacon{6%slices}(cut in 1/2-in lardons) in a cold #skillet{} over medium heat for ~render{8%min}.

>> step: boil 7 min, chill hard
Boil @eggs{2%large} for ~boil{7%min}, then ~chill{5%min} them in ice water.

>> step: sear 5 min in the fat
Sear @cremini mushrooms{8%oz}(225 g; sliced thick) in @&(~2)bacon and its fat{} over high heat for ~sear{5%min} without stirring for the first two.

>> step: whisk into the hot pan
Whisk @red wine vinegar{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @dijon mustard{1%tsp}, @light brown sugar{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)hot skillet{} off the heat, scraping the brown from the bottom.

>> step: peel and halve
Peel and halve @&(~3)chilled eggs{}.

>> step: wilt under the dressing
Wilt @baby spinach{8%cups}(200 g) and @red onion{1/4%small}(sliced paper thin) in a wide #bowl{} under @&(~2)hot dressing{}, tossing once, then set @&(~1)halved eggs{} on top.

Pour it over in one go and toss once — twice and it is cooked spinach. Half collapsed and half still raw.
